//! Fused multiply-add, x*y + z rounded once, for f64 and, suffixed f, f32; in integer arithmetic, not by the
//! hardware's instruction, so that it is musl's anywhere. Being correctly rounded, the instruction gives the same
//! bits, and is the fast path once bober's backend has it as an intrinsic.
//!
